    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cūrietae</span></b> , ārum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the inhabitants of Curieta, an island on the coast of
			Illyria</i>, now <i>Veglia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 21,
				25, § 139</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cūrietĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of Curieta</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					4, 2, 31</span></i>
			.</div>
